> [Jeremy] Stoller (Resident Dram[aturg] at the Jewish Plays Project)[ is a freelance] dram[aturg] and producer. He also serves as resident dram[atur]g for terraNOVA Collective's Groundbreakers writers group and literary consultant for Luna Stage. Founder, The Dram[atur]gy Open Office Hour Project. Past: general manager; THE GOLEM OF HAVANA workshop production @ La MaMa; literary manager, Two River Theater (2010[-]2013[);] dram[atur]gy/literary work with The Flea, Disney Theatrical Group, PlayPenn, 52nd Street Project, Target Margin, First Person Arts Festival, George Street Playhouse. He received his BA from Drew University.
